Pinned upstream commit: 984023d. The port (tools/port/port.mjs) reproduces
content/ from this exact snapshot; re-running it against the same commit
reproduces content/ byte-identically.

Documents excluded from the port (10): these describe Claude Code's own
extension points and have no DeepSeek Harness meaning, so rewriting them
would produce plausible-looking instructions for machinery that does not
exist here — worse than omitting them. Also recorded in the port manifest.
  - CLAUDE-local-template.md — template for a personal CLAUDE.local.md
    override file; a Claude Code config file this harness does not have.
  - settings-local-template.md — template for a personal
    .claude/settings.local.json; a Claude Code settings file this harness
    does not have.
  - setup-requirements.md — Claude Code install/setup instructions end to
    end (npm install -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code, hook prerequisites);
    not applicable to this harness.
  - hooks-reference.md — overview of the 12 Claude Code PreToolUse/
    PostToolUse hooks; this harness has no hook-interception seam.
  - hooks-reference/hook-input-schemas.md — JSON schemas for Claude Code
    hook stdin payloads; no hook runtime here to receive them.
  - hooks-reference/post-merge-asset-validation.md — reference doc for one
    specific upstream hook script; not portable, see hooks-reference.md above.
  - hooks-reference/post-sprint-retrospective.md — same.
  - hooks-reference/pre-commit-code-quality.md — same.
  - hooks-reference/pre-commit-design-check.md — same.
  - hooks-reference/pre-push-test-gate.md — same.

Summary of changes from the upstream work:
  - Ported from the Claude Code agent/skill/hook/rule extension points to
    the DeepSeek Harness skill registry and subagent seam.
  - Tool names rewritten to the harness vocabulary (Read -> read,
    Task -> subagent, and so on).
  - The 49 agent definitions became role briefs read by delegated
    subagents; they are no longer named agent types.
  - The 73 skills were renamed with a gs- prefix and marked
    human-invocable only.
  - The 12 hooks were NOT ported as executable hooks. The harness has no
    pre-tool-use interception; they became checklists, approval gates, and
    (later) reminder injection. They cannot block an action.
